"CVPR 2023 Open Access Repository (https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/html/He_FastInst_A_Simple_Query-Based_Model_for_Real-Time_Instance_Segmentation_CVPR_2023_paper.html)\nciteturn167search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Code can be found at https://github.com/junjiehe96/FastInst. ... @InProceedings{He_2023_CVPR, author = {He, Junjie and Li, Pengyu and Geng, Yifeng and Xie, Xuansong}, title = {FastInst: A Simple Query-Based Model for Real-Time Instance Segmentation}, booktitle = {Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)}, month = {June}, year = {2023}, pages = {23663-23672} }\n\nFastInst: A Simple Query-Based Model for Real-Time Instance Segmentation     \n\nJunjie He, Pengyu Li, Yifeng Geng, Xuansong Xie; Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023, pp. 23663-23672\n\nAbstract\n\nRecent attention in instance segmentation has focused on query-based models. Despite being non-maximum suppression (NMS)-free and end-to-end, the superiority of these models on high-accuracy real-time benchmarks has not been well demonstrated. In this paper, we show the strong potential of query-based models on efficient instance segmentation algorithm designs. We present FastInst, a simple, effective query-based framework for real-time instance segmentation. FastInst can execute at a real-time speed (i.e., 32.5 FPS) while yielding an AP of more than 40 (i.e., 40.5 AP) on COCO test-dev without bells and whistles. Specifically, FastInst follows the meta-architecture of recently introduced Mask2Former. Its key designs include instance activation-guided queries, dual-path update strategy, and ground truth mask-guided learning, which enable us to use lighter pixel decoders, fewer Transformer decoder layers, while achieving better performance. The experiments show that FastInst outperforms most state-of-the-art real-time counterparts, including strong fully convolutional baselines, in both speed and accuracy. Code can be found at https://github.com/junjiehe96/FastInst.\n\nRelated Material\n    [pdf] [supp] [arXiv]\n\n[bibtex]\n\n@InProceedings{He_2023_CVPR, author = {He, Junjie and Li, Pengyu and Geng, Yifeng and Xie, Xuansong}, title = {FastInst: A Simple Query-Based Model for Real-Time Instance Segmentation}, booktitle = {Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)}, month = {June}, year = {2023}, pages = {23663-23672} }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - nv-tlabs/GSCNN: Gated-Shape CNN for Semantic Segmentation (ICCV 2019) · GitHub (https://github.com/nv-tlabs/GSCNN)\nciteturn167search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; This is the official code for:#### Gated-SCNN: Gated Shape CNNs for Semantic Segmentation ...     git clone https://github.com/nv-tlabs/GSCNN\n\n## Folders and files\n\nName  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n\n## Latest commit\n\n \n\n## History\n\n22 Commits\ndatasets  | datasets  |    |  \ndocs  | docs  |    |  \nmy_functionals  | my_functionals  |    |  \nnetwork  | network  |    |  \ntransforms  | transforms  |    |  \nutils  | utils  |    |  \nDockerfile  | Dockerfile  |    |  \nLICENSE  | LICENSE  |    |  \nREADME.md  | README.md  |    |  \nconfig.py  | config.py  |    |  \nloss.py  | loss.py  |    |  \noptimizer.py  | optimizer.py  |    |  \ntrain.py  | train.py  |    |  \n[Button: View all files]\n\n## Repository files navigation\n\n  *   * README\n  * License\n\nMore items\n\n# GSCNN\n\nThis is the official code for:\n\n#### Gated-SCNN: Gated Shape CNNs for Semantic Segmentation\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFastInst: A Simple Query-Based Model for Real-Time Instance Segmentation (https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08594)\nciteturn167academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; Date: Wed Mar 15 13:06:30 2023 .